{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-unstable-atom-decay-channel","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel","kind":"proposition","title":"Uniqueness of the decay channel off the boundary variety","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-unstable-atom"],"tags":["decay","instability","ilp","phase-boundary"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.BraidKnot.UnstableAtom.decay_channel","text":"unstable-atom-decay-channel.md","leanSource":"unstable-atom-decay-channel.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:unstable-atom-decay-channel\"></a><p><em>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> be an atom-knot that is <a href=\"#def:unstable-atom\" data-at=\"knots-particles-confinement/atom-isotope-knots\">unstable</a> at <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code>, and let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda^*</code> be a candidate decay channel. Assume <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> lies off the boundary variety, and assume the LP-duality selection input of <a href=\"#prop:mass-coefficient-shadow-price\" data-at=\"mass-theory/substrate-binding-setup\">the shadow-price proposition</a>: off the boundary variety, every partition that minimises the constraint-violation energy equals <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda^*</code>. Then:</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li><em>any two energy-minimising partitions coincide, so the minimiser, when one exists, is unique;</em></li>\n<li><em>if the energy <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E(\\lambda^*, \\cdot)</code> is continuous on <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[q_1, q_2]</code> with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E(\\lambda^*, q_1) \\le 0 \\le E(\\lambda^*, q_2)</code>, then <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">E(\\lambda^*, q^*) = 0</code> for some <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q^* \\in [q_1, q_2]</code>.</em></li>\n</ol>\n<p><em>The existence of <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\lambda^*</code> is not part of this statement.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unstable-atom-decay-channel.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"13.21.18","page":"b/prop-unstable-atom-decay-channel","qa":{"counts":{"pass":95,"fail":2,"warn":1,"na":19,"unknown":0,"stale":93},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:BraidKnotOctonion.UnstableAtom.decay_channel","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/unstable-atom-decay-channel.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
